{"id": "EUVD-2026-108724", "enisaUuid": "76b65735-b46c-3fa9-84e9-92453aac7bbc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nworkqueue: Fix NULL current_pwq deref in chained work check\n\ncurrent_wq_worker() only tells us that %current is a kworker. It does\nnot guarantee that the worker is currently executing a work item, as\nworker->current_pwq is populated only while process_one_work() is running\nthe work function.\n\nis_chained_work() can be reached while queueing on a draining or\ndestroying workqueue. If a kworker outside work-item execution reaches\nthat path, current_wq_worker() returns a worker but worker->current_pwq is\nNULL, and the chained-work test can fault before it emits the intended\nwarning.\n\nGuard the chained-work test with worker->current_pwq. A kworker without\ncurrent_pwq is not executing work on the target workqueue, so the helper\nshould return false and let the draining/destroying warning fire.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:22:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:22:45", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3dc61af2998cfc7312d6e59bbdcd5eed074483f2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/729d576df89c7e4341e58c452f8890620a610ac2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b12a25fb2b9d5dac80e419d695450cc17a51fdfd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1a2668682e998039a027796b236319b380078a6a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/980db94e3eeefdd8a1c46f86412c33a7f7806f51"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99058"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01b02806-c290-3edc-a13d-72f5702350a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "029b23dd-bfa9-3c92-bd83-47150fce25e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "0bf64c3d-5933-3acb-8140-8187a4c525c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.9"}, {"id": "10a78d71-1ef7-3815-9124-32903f0eb97c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "46c76923-6720-3e5f-879d-653b8ef49f83", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8d03ecfe471802d6afe97da97722b6924533aa82 <1a2668682e998039a027796b236319b380078a6a"}, {"id": "7063572f-656d-3672-a615-39031df67020", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "708a4708-011a-365e-bd63-40c19d1595f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8d03ecfe471802d6afe97da97722b6924533aa82 <b12a25fb2b9d5dac80e419d695450cc17a51fdfd"}, {"id": "79e9d1dd-8caa-37eb-ab17-7e3e2a6ad85d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "8ea0fdae-5c3b-3566-a2a6-661b3c6fdb7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8d03ecfe471802d6afe97da97722b6924533aa82 <980db94e3eeefdd8a1c46f86412c33a7f7806f51"}, {"id": "d14943b7-7082-3c75-ac72-1e6e101ef889", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8d03ecfe471802d6afe97da97722b6924533aa82 <729d576df89c7e4341e58c452f8890620a610ac2"}, {"id": "d5c5a9a7-5371-331a-b47a-4e768704f9e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8d03ecfe471802d6afe97da97722b6924533aa82 <3dc61af2998cfc7312d6e59bbdcd5eed074483f2"}, {"id": "dd160a2e-a199-3c4e-bf7b-39cd04386a30", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f7913ea8-3915-38b9-b4be-086d5fd26610", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}